<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Visit Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Visit Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-visitgermany</id><updated>2026-09-05T18:26:08Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-visitgermany" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-7550?maca=en-rss-en-visitgermany-3324-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-visitgermany" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Is sustainable travel possible in times of mass tourism?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76ad4538f939943963d1407c4f84ccfc0bb983e6a547cae90214832fc5825237</id><updated>2026-09-05T18:26:08Z</updated><published>2026-02-25T09:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-sustainable-travel-possible-in-times-of-mass-tourism/a-75960699--3ae1d73f7df1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-sustainable-travel-possible-in-times-of-mass-tourism/a-75960699?maca=en-rss-en-visitgermany-3324-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Travel can drive overtourism, contribute to climate change and support problematic political systems. Yet the industry also creates livelihoods and fosters exchange.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>From boom to burden: How overtourism hit European cities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca0ce89e3d75602cafcf04e0545598d22642e0ef7a7abed08697840a80fcac3b</id><updated>2026-09-05T18:26:08Z</updated><published>2026-02-18T12:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/from-boom-to-burden-how-overtourism-hit-european-cities/a-75834155--7c9ded1f269a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/from-boom-to-burden-how-overtourism-hit-european-cities/a-75834155?maca=en-rss-en-visitgermany-3324-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Many destinations are groaning under the strain of vacationers. So what turns certain places into tourist magnets? It isn't just the famous landmarks.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Ryanair faces massive fine in Italy over 'abusive strategy'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88bcd5e544dda6ba1d107003ec31df4d94b007a8e48b46a6e039adb1adc73642</id><updated>2026-09-05T18:26:08Z</updated><published>2025-12-23T11:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ryanair-faces-massive-fine-in-italy-over-abusive-strategy/a-75282204--45996db36ea9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ryanair-faces-massive-fine-in-italy-over-abusive-strategy/a-75282204?maca=en-rss-en-visitgermany-3324-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Italy's competition authority AGCM claims the budget airline blocked payment methods and mass-deleted accounts to manipulate travel agencies and force them into partnerships. Ryanair has pledged to appeal the fine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea's Kim Jong Un, daughter open luxury resort</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f034035e3bdb4473eaa69608afed770eb952a0f3abd2bbc99ef3c0a9df196926</id><updated>2026-09-05T18:26:08Z</updated><published>2025-12-23T10:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-daughter-open-luxury-resort/a-75280175--8bce8740a562.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-daughter-open-luxury-resort/a-75280175?maca=en-rss-en-visitgermany-3324-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Five new hotels were opened in Samjiyon, near the Chinese border, with Kim Jong Un praising the "rising status" of North Korea's people.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>IndiGo's woes: Indian airline ordered to cut flights by 5%</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:658409acee28cdc932978e6dca1653089b218eb81b9458083d71706a5910309b</id><updated>2026-09-05T18:26:08Z</updated><published>2025-12-09T10:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indigo-s-woes-indian-airline-ordered-to-cut-flights-by-5/a-75073906--814009891103.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indigo-s-woes-indian-airline-ordered-to-cut-flights-by-5/a-75073906?maca=en-rss-en-visitgermany-3324-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indian aviation regulators told IndiGo to immediately reduce flights by 5%. The move comes after over 2,000 cancellations last week when it emerged pilots were not receiving sufficient time to rest between flights.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>IndiGo cancellations snarl India's air travel for fourth day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5950b3899a0fd2f073573fc10428d28868d25d43988727bc2c33db2741e398f0</id><updated>2026-09-05T18:26:08Z</updated><published>2025-12-05T11:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indigo-cancellations-snarl-india-s-air-travel-for-fourth-day/a-75032235--0dafe4fe2210.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indigo-cancellations-snarl-india-s-air-travel-for-fourth-day/a-75032235?maca=en-rss-en-visitgermany-3324-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Air travel in India has been crippled for a fourth day as the budget airline IndiGo cancelled hundreds of flights across the country. The carrier has been blamed for failing to plan for new safety rules.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mallorca sees record tourism despite protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44f11502ab9cb708c355197a07f66f37f92ae16ec57581b1290919014218a68c</id><updated>2026-09-05T18:26:08Z</updated><published>2025-09-25T08:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mallorca-sees-record-tourism-despite-protests/a-74002095--ea6ae7f57f38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mallorca-sees-record-tourism-despite-protests/a-74002095?maca=en-rss-en-visitgermany-3324-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Mediterranean island looks set to hit a new visitor record in 2025 — despite growing anti-tourist sentiment.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria debates air rage 'double standards' after woman remanded for assaulting Ibom Air crew and ground staff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5ad7ea74eb9726fc6e1ed4785365d5110963ca9fbf23a082cbf60b3e17301bc</id><updated>2026-09-05T18:26:08Z</updated><published>2025-08-12T10:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-debates-air-rage-double-standards-after-woman-remanded-for-assaulting-ibom-air-crew-and-grou/a-73611972--7f8a55b37e0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-debates-air-rage-double-standards-after-woman-remanded-for-assaulting-ibom-air-crew-and-ground-staff/a-73611972?maca=en-rss-en-visitgermany-3324-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A woman was taken into custody for allegedly assaulting airline staff, while a well-known musician who disrupted a flight remains free.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Traveling through Europe: What LGBTQIA+ people should be aware of</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:056f1e67f5622ceeb65fb97022c556217de517e80a85b6f8bee174313087dcdf</id><updated>2026-09-05T18:26:08Z</updated><published>2025-07-24T10:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/traveling-through-europe-what-lgbtqia-people-should-be-aware-of/a-73394296--0d6819fc3290.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/traveling-through-europe-what-lgbtqia-people-should-be-aware-of/a-73394296?maca=en-rss-en-visitgermany-3324-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Europe is known as a continent of diversity. For LGBTQIA+ people, there are nevertheless a few things to bear in mind when traveling.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>UNESCO: New World Heritage Sites to be announced</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f47544f71f59cb6a8be76b